FEATURE: component-teardown
DATE: 2026-09-17
PRIOR STATE: as left by feature 'resizer-docs'

REASON (applies to both changes below)
$$.attachEventHandler() delegated every handler to a listener bound on window, and
kept no reference to the closure it created. Nothing could ever be passed to
removeEventListener(), so every delegated handler in the library was permanently
bound for the life of the page. This is the reason vUX-resizer.js binds its own
named listeners instead of using the helper (see the comment at its addEventHanler()).

The helper now keeps the listener in a local, binds that, and returns a handle whose
detach() removes it again. The return value is additive: the six components that
already called the helper and ignored its result are unaffected, and every component
that now implements destroy() stores the handle instead.

This had to land before the destroy() pass, because without it a component using the
helper has no way to unbind what it registered.

